      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5a7ac88bf5a5c52c08064fb9|full_name}: While to some degree valid, there is no harm in requesting the vrc team do more in terms of mitigating exactly what you are brushing off as a phase. Why would you blindly run into the fire knowing how much you would be hurt when you have had so much time to prepare and many voices requesting more be done for their safety before they run through that same fire.\nJust a phase is not an appropriate response to a known danger. Yes you may still live after running through that fire, after the phase is over, but knowing you did nothing to avoid the damage is beyond ridiculous.",
