  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-11-20T03:29:52.709Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The concept of vrchat plus is fine, but allowing only plus users to use custom icons is going to seriously harm the community. Even the slightest bit of visual differentiation that signifies difference between plus and non-plus accounts will split the community and can cause situations like \"I'm a vrchat plus user! See that custom icon? I'm better than you!\"\nNot to meniton custom icons can be abused for inappropriate imagery. We already have avatars that can be abused, don't add in another tool for people to abuse.\nI highly suggest keeping the icons preset and predefined by the developers, like the default steam profile pictures or the ones on xbox live. They also need to be usable by both regular and plus users (perhaps have a minority of them exclusive to plus users). Maybe have the community have a bit of influence by making icon contests and contest winners having a sparkly animated version of their winning icon just for them, like community quality Team Fortress 2 items.\nI've been peeking into the VRChat official Discord server and people and crashers/ modded client users are already planning on doing targeted harassment towards plus users. This is what I'm saying! People who buy plus will be targeted by crashers and get harassed for just being a plus user! EVERY VISUAL IDENTIFIER OF VRCHAT PLUS NEEDS TO BE HIDDEN",
